      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T15:20:14Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): the tool list has one header row and one search box\n\nThe tool list of the tool library window (U9 of #3663) gets one header\nrow: the source tabs (Document, My library, Catalog), one search box\n(\"Filter by name, diameter or part number\"), then New tool…, Import…\nand Export…. Import… opens a menu with the import mode, \"Import tool\nholders\" and the file button.\n\nThe search splits the text into terms; each term must match the name,\nthe type, the category, a diameter (within 0.05 mm, in the document's\nunit), the holder, the tool number, the part number or the vendor. It\nworks the same in Document, Catalog and My library. \"N of M tools\"\nheads the rows, Esc clears the box. State keeps the rows and the hits,\nkeyed on the document version, the text and the unit, so a still frame\nbuilds nothing.\n\nThe category rail lists every category with the count of the matching\nrows. Document and Catalog rows share the columns of the mockup, with\nthe Recipes count and the \"in document\" mark. The Tool type combo is\ngone; the rail and the search do its work.\n\nFixes #4335\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
